From 708b8d91e19dfe0e87b5feae77347e9f8b10c27b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:35:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(studio): restore correct Sanity schema matching live
 site architecture
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Studio was wired to studio/schemas/ (sanity.config.ts imported from
there), but that folder was an old, incompatible schema: field names like
department.name/description, testimonial.name/quote(plain), radioProgram
.schedule, project.status/body, and siteSettings.title/socialLinks bore no
resemblance to what the live frontend actually queries (icon/title/desc
/link for department cards, localized quote/author/avatar for testimonials,
heroSlides/stats/contact/radio/partners for site settings, etc). Every one
of these content types was therefore non-functional in Sanity Studio even
though the frontend had working CMS-integration code waiting for it.

studio/schemaTypes/ (never imported anywhere, dead code) turned out to be
the correct, complete schema — same field names, same localized
(en/fr/rw) structure the frontend's pageContent.ts, cmsContent.ts,
siteSettings.ts and sanityNews.ts already expect, including a fully-built
"Secretariat Page" type that had no schema registered at all before this.

Changes:
- Promote studio/schemaTypes/ to studio/schemas/ (single source of truth);
  delete the old incompatible studio/schemas/.
- Register secretariatPage in sanity.config.ts (was completely missing
  from the Studio despite the frontend's useSecretariatPage() hook).
- Rename galleryEvent -> galleryCollection to match the frontend's
  `_type == "galleryCollection"` query and the existing Studio nav item.
- Rename newsPost's `coverImage` field -> `mainImage` to match the
  frontend query and already-published news documents (avoids
  reintroducing the exact bug fixed in an earlier deploy).
- Remove a stray `lucide-react` icon import in departmentResourceGroup.ts
  that isn't a Studio dependency and would have broken `sanity build`.

Net effect: every CMS section staff can already reach from the live
site's code (hero slider, stats, departments, testimonials, radio
schedule, projects, gallery, member churches, About/Departments/
Secretariat page copy, department resource groups & files) now has a
matching, usable Sanity Studio form.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
